From c5c70d527da9044e2724c15ebd38625079ab42bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 14:16:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CI deploy: bump workflow Node to 22 (wrangler 4.x
 requires it)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The workflow pinned Node 20, but package.json's wrangler ^4.20.0 needs
Node >=22. On Node 20, cloudflare/wrangler-action's own compatibility
fallback silently installed wrangler 3.90.0 instead, which fails to
read wrangler.jsonc's `main` field ("Missing entry-point"). This broke
the first real CI deploy since the repo was scaffolded, unrelated to
the HRPT/D1 work — the live Worker itself was unaffected since it was
already deployed manually with a properly-versioned local wrangler.
---
 .github/workflows/deploy.yml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/deploy.yml b/.github/workflows/deploy.yml
index e7eb0e7..3863ba6 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/deploy.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/deploy.yml
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@ jobs:
       - name: Setup Node.js
         uses: actions/setup-node@v4
         with:
-          node-version: 20
+          node-version: 22
 
       - name: Install dependencies
         run: npm install
-- 
2.43.0

